{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAs7Nc8oVfbpT7atPbfJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The job fails every night for two reasons, and the first one is why you never got a failure message. Both fixes are in the snapshot. I haven't loaded anything into your real launchd, so the changes need to be copied over and reloaded on your machine. The commands are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why it was silent**\n\n1. **The script killed itself before it could report.** `status=$?` in `bin/nightly-review.zsh` fails because `status` is a read-only variable in zsh. The script exits at that line, so the Telegram failure message never runs. The error log has one `read-only variable: status` line per night.\n2. **Claude could not log in under launchd.** Every run logs `Not logged in · Please run /login`. The plist sets only `PATH`, so the CLI has no `USER` to find its keychain login. No review was ever produced.\n\nlaunchd is not the problem. `runs = 6` matches six nights, 13–18 Oct.\n\n**What I changed**\n\n- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`: renamed `status` to `rc`, closed stdin for `claude`, treat empty output as a failure, and include the run duration in the message.\n- `bin/notify.sh`: fail loudly if the keychain lookup or token is empty, and use `curl -f`. Without `-f`, a rejected Telegram request exits 0 and the failure is hidden. I checked that against a local server. This didn't cause tonight's silence, but it would hide the next failure.\n- The plist: added `HOME`, `USER` and `LOGNAME`.\n\n**Checked here:** the plist lints, all scripts pass syntax checks, and the job logic runs correctly with a fake `claude` and fake notifier for success, failure and empty output.\n\n**Not verified:**\n- That `claude` authenticates under launchd. The `USER` fix is the most likely cause, not a confirmed one.\n- That a real Telegram message arrives. I didn't call Telegram or the Claude API.\n\n**Check before loading:** I set the username to `vk`, based on the `/Users/vk` paths in your plist and logs. Run `id -un` first. If it differs, change the three values.\n\nFiles are in `/private/tmp/h-oM9Vdh/`:\n- ANSWER.md\n- bin/nightly-review.zsh\n- bin/notify.sh\n- Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2701,"cache_read_input_tokens":42743,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2701},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bcf3afd4-ab3d-46b9-9d25-8bfe1d5aaa11","uuid":"ea4b28cc-8ae3-453d-8d50-6615630bb5ec","timestamp":"2026-10-19T03:12:25.948Z","request_id":"req_011CgAs7NLFtrrwMT5TE4Seo"}
